  "question": {
    "text": "Two straight roads <math><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi></math> intersect at <math><mi>O</mi></math>. A tower is situated within the angle formed by them and subtends angles of <math><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> at the points <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> where the roads are nearest to it. If <math><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math> meters and&nbsp;<math><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math> meters, then the height of the tower is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>25</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math> meters",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>50</mn></math> meters",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>25</mn><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></math> meters",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>25</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> meters",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0001_6cba5f644fb6.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.82708in;height:1.44653in\" /><br />Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> be the tower of height <math><mi>h</mi></math>.</p><p>Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math> be perpendiculars from <math><mi>P</mi></math> upon <math><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi></math> respectively.<br />Then, <math><mi>&#8736;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><mi>&#8736;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cot</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cot</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>h</mi></math><br />Now, <math><mi>O</mi><msup><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><msup><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></math> meters</p>"
  }
